-- a LowCardinality-typed key under CUBE: `if` can never return LowCardinality, so the
-- correcting conditional would narrow the declared type. Such a key is declined (the firing
-- assertion below reads 0) and the result stays unoptimized but correct. Without the decline
-- the enclosing length()/hex() is handed the narrowed type and the query fails to analyze.
lc cube on		0	2
lc cube on	ba	2	1
lc cube on	dc	2	1
lc cube off		0	2
lc cube off	ba	2	1
lc cube off	dc	2	1
-- and the declared type must not depend on the setting (both arms report LowCardinality(String))
k	LowCardinality(String)					
k	LowCardinality(String)					
