-- HAVING over the eliminated key. The predicate is evaluated after aggregation, so it must see
-- the corrected value: HAVING k = \'\' selects the subtotal row, and HAVING k = \'0\' must not.
-- Each is paired with its optimization-disabled oracle. Every row carries its own label: the
-- two CUBE cells are complementary, so an unlabelled pair would let a row lost by one and a row
-- gained by the other cancel out in the line diff.
cube-empty		3
cube-empty off		3
cube-zero	0	1
cube-zero off	0	1
