-- per-modifier firing assertion: 1 means the unwrap actually happened (no injective function is
-- left in the GROUP BY section of the analyzed tree). Without this the assertions above would
-- also pass if the optimization silently declined for every modifier.
CUBE	1
ROLLUP	1
GROUPING SETS	1
ROLLUP WITH TOTALS	1
-- plain WITH TOTALS reads 0: it is DECLINED on purpose (its correction cannot survive the
-- conversion of the query tree to an AST). The grouping-set modifiers above still read 1.
WITH TOTALS declined	0
-- the same assertion reads 0 when the optimization is off, so it is not vacuous
CUBE off	0
-- firing assertions for the four special-path shapes above, whose other assertions compare
-- results against the optimization-disabled arm and would therefore also pass if the pass had
-- silently declined for that shape. The window is the GROUP BY SECTION only (up to the next
-- section header), because the correction deliberately puts toString back into ORDER BY /
-- INTERPOLATE / the projection. Each is paired with its own off arm, which must read 0.
self-join	1
self-join off	0
user grouping()	1
user grouping() off	0
LIMIT BY	1
LIMIT BY off	0
INTERPOLATE	1
INTERPOLATE off	0
HAVING	1
HAVING off	0
-- the constant-key decline is targeted: the shape with a constant key reads 0 (declined) while a
-- sibling with the SAME predicate whose second key is a non-constant function still reads 1, so
-- the decline has not silently disabled the whole modifier family.
constant key declined	0
non-constant sibling fires	1
constant key declined, GROUPING SETS	0
-- the LowCardinality key reads 0 (declined by the type-preservation gate) while the same shape
-- over a plain String column reads 1, so the gate is targeted at the type that `if` narrows.
lc key declined	0
non-lc sibling fires	1
-- and the FixedString wrapper under CUBE fires, so its subtotal really comes from the correction
fixed string cube fires	1
-- every firing assertion above inherits force_grouping_standard_compatibility = 1 from the
-- file-level SET, but the grouping conditional compares against a different constant on the other
-- branch. This pair covers it: a silent decline there would still produce correct results, so the
-- reference diff alone cannot catch it.
compatibility 0 fires	1
compatibility 0 off	0
